      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Bethamcherla</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The destination delivery handover for two-wheelers and motorcycles is a crucial process that ensures the vehicle is delivered in the same condition as when it was picked up. This process involves a thorough re-inspection of the vehicle under daylight conditions, verification of the odometer reading, and a signed condition sign-off.</p>

<p>The re-inspection process involves checking the vehicle against the pickup photos taken at the time of pickup. This includes checking for any scratches, dents, or other damages that may have occurred during transit. The inspection is done under daylight conditions to ensure that any damage is easily visible.</p>

<p>The odometer verification is done by checking the current reading against the reading mentioned in the LR bilty (Lorry Receipt). This ensures that the vehicle has not been used excessively during transit, which could lead to additional wear and tear.</p>

<p>The signed condition sign-off is a critical step in the handover process. The recipient is required to sign a document that confirms the condition of the vehicle at the time of delivery.</p>
<p>This document includes details of any damages or issues found during the re-inspection, as well as the odometer reading. The signed document serves as proof that the vehicle was delivered in the same condition as when it was picked up.</p>

